WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.367
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.330
SPEAKER: Hi.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:12.660
Today, I'm here to tell you all
about Google Cloud's Transfer

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:16.680
Appliance, an easy, secure, and
performant way to physically

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.260
ship your data to the cloud.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.690
Transfer Appliance was
created for customers

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.940
needing to transfer
large amounts of data

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.530
to Google Cloud.

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:28.410
Large-scale data transfers
done over the wire

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:31.410
require network connections
with sufficient bandwidth.

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:34.860
And some customers aren't
able to procure or dedicate

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.050
that kind of bandwidth
without disrupting

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.300
their critical
business operations.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:42.630
When an online data transfer
isn't feasible, preferable,

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:44.970
or efficient, the
Transfer Appliance

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:47.940
is the best way to make
a large data transfer.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.310
But how does it work?

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.500
We ship you an appliance.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.930
You upload your data.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:58.440
You ship the appliance back
to a Google upload facility.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:02.850
And voila, your data is
available in Google Cloud.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.000
The appliance itself is
about the size of a suitcase,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.060
and is easy to move
exactly where you need it.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:13.590
And Transfer Appliance comes
in two capacities, 40 terabytes

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:16.110
and 300 terabytes.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:19.590
And any time we're talking about
moving large amounts of data,

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.560
security is the
number-one priority.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:26.220
This device is tamper-resistant
and sealed during shipment,

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.740
and is designed to
protect your data.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.590
Transfer Appliance was designed
so that everything you need

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.840
is on board the device itself.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.720
When preparing to upload
your data to the appliance,

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.670
you'll connect it
to your network.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:41.910
The on-device display and
included setup guide will

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:44.190
walk you through the process.

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:47.460
To start, power on the device.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.890
Configure for your network.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:52.510
Begin capturing data.

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:54.840
Once your transfer is
complete, the device

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.750
is ready to ship back to
a Google upload facility.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.700
And for customers
who prefer to place

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:03.090
inside a data-center rack, we
have a rackable form factor

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:05.400
available that can
be placed on a shelf.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.770
Once we receive it,
we upload the data

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.860
into your Cloud Storage
bucket, then wipe the appliance

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:12.330
when we're done.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:15.330
Your data is now
available in Google Cloud.

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:18.420
Now you can take advantage
of our powerful analytics

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:21.660
or machine-learning tools,
or simply back up your data

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.760
in case you need it later.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.430
Transfer Appliance is
a great fit for data

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:29.820
collection from researchers,
vendors, or other sites

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:31.290
to Google Cloud.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:32.700
Data replication.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.920
Take advantage of
hybrid architectures

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.050
and keep your on-prem
infrastructure

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:40.440
while also experimenting with
the powerful data-analysis

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.360
tools Google offers.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:43.770
Data migration.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.810
Move large amounts
of existing data

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:48.780
to ultra-low-cost
archival storage.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:51.120
To see if the Transfer
Appliance is right for you,

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.929
check out cloud.google.com.

